Let $P$ be the set of all polynomials with integer coefficients and positive degree. For any two distinct polynomials $f$ and $g$ in $P$, define the function $h_{f,g} : \mathbb{N} \to \mathbb{Z}$ by
\[ h_{f,g}(n) = \begin{cases} 
1 & \text{if } f(n) \equiv 0 \pmod{g(n)} \\
0 & \text{otherwise}
\end{cases} \]
for all natural numbers $n$. Determine the maximum possible cardinality of a subset $S$ of $P$ such that for any pair of distinct polynomials $f, g \in S$, there exists no positive integer $n$ for which $h_{f,g}(n) = 1$ and $h_{g,f}(n) = 1$ simultaneously.

