An equilateral triangle  $ABE$  is inscribed in the square  $ABCD$  so that  $E$  lies on side  $CD$ .  Point  $M$  is the midpoint of  $AE$  and points  $H$  and  $I$  lie on the sides  $AD$  and  $BC$ , respectively, so that  $HI$  is parallel to  $AB$  and contains  $M$ . If the area of quadrilateral  $HIEA$  is 24 , find the area of the square  $ABCD$ .

[asy]
unitsize(3 cm);

pair A, B, C, D, E, H, I, M;

D = (0,0);
C = (1,0);
B = (1,1);
A = (0,1);
E = extension(B, midpoint(D--C),A,D);
I = extension(H, M, B, C);
M = midpoint(A--E);

draw(A--B--C--D--cycle);
draw(B--E);
draw(H--I);

label(" $A$ ", A, W);
label(" $B$ ", B, NE);
label(" $C$ ", C, E);
label(" $D$ ", D, SW);
label(" $E$ ", E, SE);
label(" $I$ ", I, E);
label(" $H$ ", H, W);
label(" $M$ ", M, N);
[/asy]

What is the smallest positive integer value of \( n \) for which there exist polynomials \( f(x) \) with integer coefficients and a polynomial \( g(x) \) with real coefficients satisfying \[
(x^2 - 1)^n = f(x) \left((x^2 - 1)^{n+1} + 1\right) + g(x) \left((x^2 - 1)^{n+1} - 1\right) \text{?}
\]

We define a function \( f: \mathbb{N} \to \mathbb{N} \) such that for every positive integer \( n \),

\[ f(n) = \begin{cases} 
      n + 1 & \text{if } n \text{ is prime} \\
      f(n - 1) & \text{otherwise}
   \end{cases}
\]

Let \( S \) be the smallest set of positive integers satisfying:

1. For any \( n \in S \), \( f(n) \in S \).
2. If \( n \in S \) and \( m \) is any divisor of \( n \), then \( m \in S \).

Determine all positive integers \( k \) such that there exists a subset \( T \subseteq S \) with \( |T| = k \) and no two elements in \( T \) are relatively prime.

