A function $f:\mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}$ satisfies for all real numbers $x, y,$ and $z$,
\begin{align*}
f(x + y + z) &= f(x) + f(y) + f(z) - 2f(x)f(y)f(z) \\
f(xyz) &= f(x)f(y)f(z) + x^2y^2z^2.
\end{align*} 
Determine the number of distinct possible values that $f$ can take on when evaluated at all integers.

Define a sequence \( a_n \) by \( a_1 = 1, a_2 = 1 \), and for \( n \geq 3 \),
\[ a_n = \begin{cases} 
a_{n-1} + a_{n-2} & \text{if } n \text{ is odd} \\
a_{n-1} \cdot a_{n-2} & \text{if } n \text{ is even} 
\end{cases} \]
Find the smallest \( n > 1 \) such that \( a_n > 10^{18} \). If no such \( n \) exists, output "No solution exists."

