Alice and Bob play a game on an infinite grid of cells. Initially, Alice draws a finite set of cells that form a connected shape (cells are adjacent if they share an edge). On her turn, Alice chooses one of her cells and draws a line segment from that cell to any adjacent empty cell. Bob then claims the cell at the endpoint of the line segment, if it exists, otherwise he claims no cell. The game ends when Alice cannot make a move. Alice wins if she has claimed exactly half of the cells she started with; otherwise, Bob wins. What is the maximum number of cells Alice can start with and still guarantee a win?

[asy]
unitsize(0.5 cm);

int i, j;

for (i = -5; i <= 5; ++i) {
for (j = -5; j <= 5; ++j) {
dot((i,j));
}
}

draw((-4,0)--(4,0),red);
draw((0,-4)--(0,4),red);
[/asy]
